SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: Understanding Brain Health
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: Health & Wellness\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 1 spot 
 left\nStatus: You are Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.c
 om/events/186163\n\n5:00PM Reception\, 5:30PM Discussion\nWhat if brain he
 alth wasn’t just clinical—but personal\, preventative\, and deeply rel
 evant to how we live every day? In honor of Alzheimer's Awareness Month\, 
 this candid\, forward-thinking conversation brings together leading physic
 ians and patient voices to explore the latest in neurovascular innovation\
 , life-saving interventions\, and the often-overlooked habits that shape c
 ognitive well-being. Expect an unfiltered look at survival\, prevention\, 
 and the science redefining how we think about the brain.\n\nFeaturing Dr. 
 Christopher Ogilvy—Director of Endovascular and Operative Neurovascular 
 Surgery at Beth Israel Deaconess Medical Center and Professor at Harvard M
 edical School—whose pioneering work continues to push the boundaries of 
 modern neurosurgery\, alongside Meg Smith\, CEO of Cure Alzheimer’s Fun
 d. Since taking the helm in 2023\, Smith has led the organization’s cont
 inued growth and impact\, advancing a research model that has directed ove
 r $138 million toward bold scientific efforts to slow\, prevent\, and ulti
 mately reverse Alzheimer’s.\n\nTogether with additional expert and patie
 nt perspectives\, the panel offers a rare opportunity to engage with leade
 rs at the forefront of brain health and discovery.\n\n*This event is compl
 imentary and reserved for members only. Light bites and refreshments will 
 be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/186163
CATEGORIES:Health & Wellness
END:VEVENT
